    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. that makes sense. i'm mostly worried about some weird edge cases though—like when users are navigating through complex data tables or when icons don't have clear labels. what are some common issues or \"hidden\" things that usually mess up the user experience in those specific areas?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In complex data tables, the most common failure point is omitting `scope` attributes in table headers, which causes screen readers to lose context when traversing rows. Regarding unlabeled icons, if an image lacks descriptive alternative text or the surrounding link is missing a label, users relying on audio often cannot distinguish clickable elements from decorative ones. Additionally, ensure that color alone isn't the only indicator of membership, such as distinguishing list items or error states, as this fails when auditory feedback is enabled.",
      "source": "target",
